; §18 stretch — keyword round-trip. The manifest binds `(echo-tag s)`
; to `:impl "wasm:tag"`, double.wasm's identity export. The evaluator
; turns the literal `:hello` into a `Value.keyword`, the codec ships
; it as tag `0x05` + length-prefixed bytes, and the plugin echoes it
; back as the same tag. A clean diagnostics stream proves the
; keyword/string codec distinction (`0x04` vs `0x05`) crosses the
; boundary intact — no JSON-style `$kw` discriminator hack. Skipped on
; Zig-native + TS-parity (no wasm runtime).
(use-plugin "double")

(echo-tag :hello)
